<title>CHILE: Endesa takes control of Colombia plant.</title>
<headline>Endesa takes control of Colombia plant.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>A consortium led by Chilean electricity utility Empresa Nacional de Electricidad (Endesa) paid $302 million Friday and took control of Colombia's Betania power plant, said Endesa.</p>
<p>The group, which is 75 percent-controlled by Endesa, bought the state-owned plant in an auction last week.</p>
<p>Betania lies 300 kilometers from Bogota and has installed capacity of 500 megawatts.</p>
<p>Endesa, Chile's largest power generator, also has investments in Argentina and Peru.</p>
<p>((-- Margaret Orgill, Santiago newsroom, 562-699-5595x212))</p>
